<p>Well, although I think this is only okay, and barely ever do Little Misters intend to kill (although I suppose the main effect is to repel, but y'know), I do have to point out&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Ms.&nbsp;Sweetie's&nbsp;Secret&nbsp;Use</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">This&nbsp;Makes&nbsp;Too&nbsp;Much&nbsp;Sense</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Thaumiel</p>
<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-2396 is to be exposed to <a href="/scp-871">SCP-871</a> daily, and instructed to consume all instances of <a href="/scp-871">SCP-871</a> in a timely manner. All escorts must be female, and male staff must maintain a 50 meter distance from SCP-2396. SCP-2396 should be kept in a normal human containment chamber at all other times.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Tell me the Foundation wouldn't do this, I mean c'mon. Anyway, this is only a neutral vote. Not a downvote, but I would really hope that the one Ms. of the group would&#8230; stand out more, and have more to do with the story of Wondertainment. As is, this is&#8230; mmmmeh. In fact, I might downvote just because Ms. Sweetie was very anticipated, and this is fairly disappointing and bland. But I have not decided yet. I guess you'll know soon.</p>

